<Item XName="READ_ME" UserName="READ_ME" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;RF Phased Array Intermods and Harmonics&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ff0000 size=2&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;This workspace demonstrates simulation of intermods and harmonics in a Phased Array Tx system. It also illustrates how to&amp;nbsp;plot intermod and harmonic spectrum, EIRP spectrum, and EIRP patterns.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Overview&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;EM&gt;TxDesign&lt;/EM&gt;&amp;nbsp;represents a simple&amp;nbsp;4x4 element phased array transmitter with&amp;nbsp;a single splitting stage. The source (&lt;EM&gt;ArrayPort2&lt;/EM&gt;) is set up to generate two tones at &lt;EM&gt;Fsignal&lt;/EM&gt; (10) and &lt;EM&gt;Fsignal&lt;/EM&gt;+1 (11) GHz (&lt;EM&gt;Fsignal&lt;/EM&gt; is a tunable variable defined in &lt;EM&gt;Constants&lt;/EM&gt; equation page). When these two tones go through the two non-linear amplifiers (&lt;EM&gt;DriverAmp&lt;/EM&gt; and &lt;EM&gt;FinalAmp&lt;/EM&gt;) intermods and harmonics will be generated. Due to the Taylor window used (&lt;EM&gt;ArrayAttn2&lt;/EM&gt;) before the first amplifier the levels of intermods and harmonics will vary for the different paths (16) in this system.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;How to setup Intermod and Harmonic simulation in Phased Array Analysis&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Generation of Intermods and Harmonics is controlled by several settings in the &lt;STRONG&gt;Options&lt;/STRONG&gt; tab of the &lt;EM&gt;PhasedArray1&lt;/EM&gt; analysis.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Check&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;Calculate Intermod and Harmonic Spectrum&lt;/STRONG&gt; to enable intermod and harmonic computation for Tx phaed array designs.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Check&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;Calculate maximum Tx&amp;nbsp;EIRP &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;at each intermod frequency&lt;/STRONG&gt; to compute the maximum (across all direction) of the EIRP (equivalent isotropically radiated power)&amp;nbsp;at each intermod frequency.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Check &lt;STRONG&gt;Report&amp;nbsp;Tx EIRP&amp;nbsp;pattern&amp;nbsp;at frequencies&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;to&amp;nbsp;save EIRP patterns at&amp;nbsp;the specified&amp;nbsp;frequencies in the dataset.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;How to Plot Intermod and Harmonic&amp;nbsp;Spectrum&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: red; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Run the simulation and open the dataset &lt;EM&gt;PhasedArray1_TxDesign_Data&lt;/EM&gt;. When &lt;STRONG&gt;Calculate Intermod and Harmonic Spectrum&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;is enabled in the Options tab of the Phased Array analysis, new&amp;nbsp;variables are created in the dataset. For example:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Spectrum_Power_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output&lt;/STRONG&gt; : this dataset variable represents the power spectrum at the output of FinalAmp_RFAmpHO, which is&amp;nbsp;the 6th&amp;nbsp;part along the&amp;nbsp;chain. The naming convention for power spectrum variable&amp;nbsp;is &lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Power_&amp;lt;N&amp;gt;_&amp;lt;Part Instance Name&amp;gt;_Output.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Spectrum_Voltage_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output&lt;/STRONG&gt; : this dataset variable represents the&amp;nbsp;voltage spectrum at the output of FinalAmp_RFAmpHO. The naming convention for&amp;nbsp;voltage spectrum variable&amp;nbsp;is &lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Voltage_&amp;lt;N&amp;gt;_&amp;lt;Part Instance Name&amp;gt;_Output.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;These variables provide Spectrasys-Spectrum-like plots for the phased array system. You can plot them by:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Right click&lt;/STRONG&gt; on&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;variable&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;Add to Graph&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;gt; New Graph&lt;/STRONG&gt;.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;For example, when you plot&amp;nbsp;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Power_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output, &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;you will see&amp;nbsp;an overlap of spectrums&amp;nbsp;for all 64 channels at the output of FinalAmp_RFAmpHO.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;You can easily plot a &lt;STRONG&gt;single channel&lt;/STRONG&gt; or a &lt;STRONG&gt;subset of channels&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;by:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Right click&lt;/STRONG&gt; on the variable &lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;gt; Add to Graph &amp;gt; New Graph of Selected Channel(s)&lt;/STRONG&gt;, then select the desired channel number.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;If the desired channel number is not shown in the dropdown, you can select the &lt;STRONG&gt;More...&lt;/STRONG&gt; option and enter the channel number. In this case you can also enter a list of numbers (e.g. 1 5 18 40) or a MATLAB Script expression evaluating to an array of integers (e.g. 1:2:20&amp;nbsp;to plot all odd-numbered channels up to 20).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;In dataset, you will also see variables like Spectrum_CH_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output, Spectrum_F_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output, Spectrum_ID_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output. They are only used as independent variables for &lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Power_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output and &lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Voltage_06_FinalAmp_RFAmpHO_Output.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;How to&amp;nbsp;Show Maximum EIRP&amp;nbsp;in Spectrum Graph&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;If &lt;STRONG&gt;Calculate maximum Tx&amp;nbsp;EIRP &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;at each intermod frequency&lt;/STRONG&gt; is&amp;nbsp;checked in the Options tab of the Phased Array analysis, then the following variable &lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;is created in the dataset.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Spectrum_Power_EIRP&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Right click&lt;/STRONG&gt; on&amp;nbsp;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Spectrum_Power_EIRP&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;Add to Graph&lt;/STRONG&gt; &lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;gt; New Graph&lt;/STRONG&gt;. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;This generates a spectrum-like plot showing the maximum (across all direction) of the EIRP for each intermod frequency. If you &lt;STRONG&gt;mouse over&lt;/STRONG&gt; the points in this graph you will see the direction (theta/phi) at which the maximum occured.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;How to Plot EIRP Patterns&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;To see the entire&amp;nbsp;EIRP pattern for select frequencies, check the &lt;STRONG&gt;Report&amp;nbsp;Tx EIRP&amp;nbsp;pattern&amp;nbsp;at frequencies&lt;/STRONG&gt; checkbox and list the desired frequencies in available field. The frequencies must be valid intermod and harmonic frequencies, otherwise they will be ignored. You can obtain the valid intermod and harmonic frequencies from the tones in&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;Spectrum_&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;EM&gt;P_EIRP&lt;/EM&gt;.&amp;nbsp;After the simulation runs, the following variables are created in the dataset:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Spectrum_EIRP_Pattern_&amp;lt;FreqValue&amp;gt;Hz&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;EM&gt; &lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;To plot these&amp;nbsp;EIRP patterns run the equation &lt;EM&gt;PlotPatterns&lt;/EM&gt;. You can follow the equations in&amp;nbsp;&lt;EM&gt;PlotPatterns&lt;/EM&gt; to plot EIRP patterns for other designs. For example:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=ltr&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;using(&apos;PhasedArray1_TxDesign_Data&apos;);&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;graph1=graph_figure(&apos;EIRP_Pattern_1e10Hz&apos;);&lt;BR&gt;graph2.add_spherical_data( Spectrum_EIRP_PhiGrid , Spectrum_EIRP_ThetaGrid, max(10*log10(Spectrum_EIRP_Pattern_1e10Hz)+30,0) );&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Observation&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;For all the parts before the first amplifier (&lt;EM&gt;DriveAmp&lt;/EM&gt;), this spectrum will only include the two input tones. At the output of the &lt;EM&gt;ArrayAttn1&lt;/EM&gt; you can see the variation of the level of these two tones due to the Taylor window applied. You can mouse over the points in this graph to see channel identification information (channel number the point corresponds to) as well as Intermod identification (what source frequencies intermodulated to create this spectral component). Since there are many points close to each other (many overlap since the Taylor window will provide the same attenuation level to several groups of channels) you may want to zoom in so that the points are separated and the mouse over will give you information only about the point you mouse over. At the output of the two amplifiers you can see the harmonics and intermods.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
